<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25239" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">jŏcŭlāris</span></b> ,
		e, adj.
		joculus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>facetious, jocular, laughable, droll</i> (class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">audacia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					Phorm. 1, 2, 84</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">joculare istuc quidem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Leg. 1, 20</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">licentia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Fat. 8</span></i>
			.—<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">jŏcŭlārĭa</span></b> ,
				ium, n.
			<i>plur., jests, jokes</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ut qui jocularia ridens Percurram,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					S. 1, 1, 23</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fundere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 7,
					2</span></i>
			.—<i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">jŏcŭlā-rĭter</span></b> ,
				<i>jocosely, in a jocular</i> or <i>comical manner</i>: irridere, Ps.-Ascon. ap. <i><span class="en">Cic. Div. in Caecin. 11, 33</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">obicere aliquid alicui,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					22, 22, 38, § 80</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">canere carmina,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Caes. 49</span></i>
			.</div>
